.TH FRDPD 8 "July 2026" "FreeRDP" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
frdpd \- FreeRDP PAM/SSSD/NLA server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B frdpd
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B frdpd
.BI --pam-auth-test " user"
.RI [ --domain " domain" ]
.RI [ --service " service" ]
.RI [ --rhost " host" ]
.RI [ --domain-mode= plain|downlevel|upn|auto ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B frdpd
accepts RDP connections using TLS and CredSSP/NLA.  In the normal service
topology it delegates authentication and account checks to
.BR frdp-authd (8)
and managed session ownership to
.BR frdp-sesmand (8).
.PP
The packaged service is deliberately not enabled or started until TLS, PAM or
SSSD policy, and the NTLM SAM (when enabled) have been provisioned.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config= path
Load the server configuration before command-line overrides.
.TP
.BI --bind= address
Override the configured listen address.
.TP
.BI --port= port
Override the configured TCP port.
.TP
.BI --max-connections= count
Limit concurrent accepted peers; zero means unlimited.
.TP
.BI --cert= path
Override the TLS certificate path.
.TP
.BI --key= path
Override the TLS private-key path.
.TP
.BI --pam-service= name
Override the PAM service name.
.TP
.BI --auth-socket= path
Override the authentication-broker socket.
.TP
.BI --session-socket= path
Override the session-manager socket.
.TP
.BI --domain-mode= plain|downlevel|upn|auto
Control how a separately supplied RDP domain is combined with the username
before PAM authentication.  Plain keeps the username unchanged; downlevel
uses DOMAIN\euser; UPN uses user@domain; and auto selects UPN when the domain
contains a dot, otherwise downlevel.  Already-qualified usernames and users
without a separate domain remain unchanged.
.TP
.B --allow-tls-fallback
Advertise TLS in addition to NLA.  NLA remains preferred.
.TP
.BI --pam-auth-test " user"
Prompt for a password and run a local PAM authentication and account-policy
smoke test without starting the listener or helper topology.
.TP
.BI --domain " domain"
Supply a separate domain to
.BR --pam-auth-test .
.TP
.BI --service " service"
Select the PAM service for
.BR --pam-auth-test .
Normal server startup uses
.BR --pam-service .
.TP
.BI --rhost " host"
Set the PAM remote-host item for
.BR --pam-auth-test .
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show command usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/frdpd/frdpd.toml
Main server and helper configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/frdpd/frdpd.env
Optional service arguments.
.TP
.I /etc/frdpd/ntlm.sam
Owner-only password-equivalent NTLM proof store for an NTLM-enabled build.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR frdp-authd (8),
.BR frdp-sesmand (8),
.BR frdpctl (1),
.BR winpr-hash (1)
